<title>CHILE: Codelco copper output rises Jan-Sept.</title>
<headline>Codelco copper output rises Jan-Sept.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Copper production at state copper firm Codelco rose 4.4 percent in the first nine months of the year to 883,600 tonnes over the same period of 1995, company figures showed.</p>
<p>All four of Codelco's mines showed increases, led by Andina, site of a major expansion project.</p>
<p>Production figures were as follows, all in metric tonnes, metal content, as provided by Codelco.</p>
<p>		     Jan-Sept 96    Jan-Sept 95  Pct increase</p>
<p> Chuquicamata     456,000	  441,000	 3.4</p>
<p> El Teniente	252,600	  238,800	 5.8</p>
<p> Andina	     115,700	  107,300	 7.8</p>
<p> Salvador	    64,900	   64,000	 1.4</p>
<p> TOTAL		883,600	  851,300	 4.4</p>
<p>Figures may not add up due to rounding.</p>
<p>--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211</p>
</text>
